From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 13:22:53 +0200
Subject: media: hm5065: Fix the flicker detection attempt count write width

The attempt count at 0x192 is a byte register, but it was written with
the 16-bit helper: the count itself got the zero high byte, which the
datasheet defines as "keep trying forever", and the 100 spilled into
the high byte of the flicker identification threshold at 0x193. So
automatic mains frequency detection never gave up and ran against a
threshold of 0x64xx instead of the firmware default.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
@@ -928,8 +928,8 @@ static int hm5065_set_power_line_frequency(struct hm5065_dev *sensor, s32 val)
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 
-		ret = hm5065_write16(sensor, HM5065_REG_FD_MAX_NUMBER_ATTEMP,
-				     100);
+		ret = hm5065_write(sensor, HM5065_REG_FD_MAX_NUMBER_ATTEMP,
+				   100);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 
